Gemini implementation contract (mandatory)
Phase 0 — truthfulness and test harness: Rename UI and engine behavior explicitly as SIMULATION, remove fabricated calibration success and synthetic recordings exported as real masters. Add CI command for test suite and FFmpeg/ffprobe decoder tests. Correct OGG encoder first.

Phase 1 — MIDI contracts: Implement standalone Windows MIDI port layer with independent MIDInes and MIDIbox SID destinations; robust MIDI import and semantic channel mapping. Fix conductor/track indexing and DPCM offset. Dispatch all required events and full panic/reset.

Phase 2 — MIDIbox SID protocol and patch schema: Build exact V2 protocol registry from official tables. Use byte-level test vectors before UI. Discriminated engine patch models, SysEx librarian and reversible serialization. Do not invent register/NRPN addresses. Start read-only protocol inspection if unsure.

Phase 3 — Full SID editor: Lead, Bassline, Multi and Drum separate screens with all documented parameters, stereo/core/instrument targets, modulation/wavetable/trigger/sequencer editors. Maintain explicit unsupported/not verified UI states; no fake interactive controls.

Phase 4 — Native audio: Build Windows ASIO backend, physical device selection, 1x mono NES + 4x SID stereo, external FX A/B sends/returns, stereo mastering chain send, real stereo master return, real calibration and feedback safety. Preserve simulator only as an explicit offline test mode.

Phase 5 — Recording/export: Stream capture from physical return to lossless WAV, convert using proven Vorbis encoder, set sample-exact RPG Maker MV OGG tags, verify decoded loop and actual MV playback. No recording -> no export.

Phase 6 — Reliability: Structured project assets, firmware/device snapshots, failure modes, recovery, unit/integration/hardware tests and regressions.
Definition of done / objective pass gates
- [ ] 4 MIDIbox SID cores addressable and connected; all 8 chip sockets profiled.
- [ ] Every supported parameter in the published V2 chart represented in one or more engine-specific editors, with documented protocol mapping and writable/readable status.
- [ ] Patch .syx read -> parse -> serialize -> compare roundtrips losslessly on known fixtures.
- [ ] All 8 main MIDI instrument lanes plus auxiliary DPCM map correctly even when SMF has a separate conductor track.
- [ ] Ordered CC/NRPN/clock + note messages emitted to proper MIDI device, observable on virtual MIDI capture.
- [ ] Two external stereo effects loops and mastering return are physically routed on actual ASIO channels, independently loopback-tested and protected from feedback.
- [ ] Master capture is verified to originate from selected hardware return, not local demo audio.
- [ ] OGG decodes in ffmpeg/ffprobe and plays in RPG Maker MV; loop tags and 10-cycle seam audition are real.
- [ ] Tests fail when protocols, routing, encoding or hardware assumptions are invalid; they do not merely check labels, headers and timer animations.
Review limitations
This is static analysis of the main branch through GitHub and cross-check against official MIDIbox SID V2 documentation. No npm install, TypeScript compilation, execution, GUI interaction, native ASIO/MIDI device, or physical synthesizer testing occurred. Line numbers are source line numbers at review time and can drift as Gemini edits code. Some missing features are intentional prototype scope; they are nonetheless blockers relative to the user's full hardware workstation requirements. This report does not claim unverified MIDIbox SID NRPN addresses are correct.